---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} uses affiliate links and advertising, and what that means for our recommendations.`}
>
  <div class="wrap page">
    <h1>Affiliate Disclosure</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        <strong>{SITE.name} is reader-supported.</strong> Some links on this site are
        affiliate links. If you click one and buy something, we may earn a commission
        from the retailer. The price you pay is exactly the same either way.
      </p>

      <h2>Which links are affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        Any link that sends you to a store to buy a product — graphics cards, prebuilt
        PCs, monitors, peripherals, and occasionally games. These are marked with a
        "Check price" button and carry a <code>rel="sponsored"</code> attribute so search
        engines can identify them. Links to other articles, official sources, patch notes
        and developer statements are never monetised.
      </p>

      <h2>Programmes we participate in</h2>
      <p>
        As an Amazon Associate we earn from qualifying purchases. We also work with other
        retailer and manufacturer affiliate programmes through affiliate networks.
      </p>

      <h2>How this affects our recommendations</h2>
      <p>
        It does not. Which product wins a buying guide is decided on testing and value
        before commission rates are considered. We routinely recommend products that pay
        us nothing, and we leave out products that pay well but do not deserve a spot.
        If a pick changes, it is because the hardware, the price or the competition
        changed.
      </p>

      <h2>Prices and availability</h2>
      <p>
        Prices shown are indicative and were accurate when the article was written or
        last updated. Retail pricing moves constantly — always confirm the current price
        on the retailer's page before you buy.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        We also run display advertising. Advertisers have no input into editorial
        content, and ad slots are kept out of the reading flow wherever we can manage it.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        If anything here is unclear, or you think a link is not properly disclosed,
        get in touch and we will correct it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    max-width: 820px;
    padding-block: 40px 20px;
  }
  .page h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.2rem);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);
    padding-bottom: 14px;
  }
</style>
